<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Exclude constrained fields from LLM arg-filling; incoherent-combo prevention</title>
    <phase>2: Structured Creation Core</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>010</dependencies>
    <blocks>none</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, backend</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies the capability input-schema path on the dispatch side; enforces the P1 invariant.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Touches how the single agent turn fills args; correctness-critical to the "LLM never emits a closed-set value" invariant.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Sequential with 010 (consumes the resolver).</parallel-reason>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    In the capability sprk_inputschema path, exclude constrained (closed-set) fields from LLM arg-filling so they are resolved by the FR-B1 resolver, not free-text LLM args. Make incoherent proposals impossible to commit — a nonsensical practice-area × matter-type pair cannot pass the grounded picker.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer expert in the SPAARKE dispatch input-schema path and ADR-039 grounded execution.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Closed-set fields are marked/excluded so the agent turn does not free-text them; the resolver (010) supplies their values. A code/test assertion proves closed-set fields are resolved by FR-B1, not LLM args. An incoherent practice-area × matter-type pair is impossible through the grounded picker.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Complements 010: the resolver provides deterministic values, and this task ensures the LLM is not asked to (and cannot) fill them. Directly closes UC-3-class failures.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">MUST NOT let the LLM emit final closed-set values; closed-set fields resolved deterministically via the resolver only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT add a second intent mechanism. Exclusion is a declarative property of the input schema / a filter over args — not a classifier.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add unit + seam coverage; the negative (incoherent-combo) case is mandatory (NFR-06 will add the eval).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Locate where capability sprk_inputschema fields are presented to the agent for arg-filling.</step>
    <step order="2">Mark closed-set fields (option-set/lookup) as resolver-owned; exclude them from the LLM-visible arg set.</step>
    <step order="3">Route those fields through the 010 resolver at dispatch/pre-seed time.</step>
    <step order="4">Add the guard that an unresolved/incoherent closed-set value cannot commit (fails to none/low → picker, never a silent bad write).</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: assertion that closed-set fields are resolver-sourced; negative test that an incoherent practice-area × matter-type pair cannot commit.</step>
    <step order="6">Build + publish-size. Update TASK-INDEX.md 011 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/ (input-schema arg-fill exclusion)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/ + tests/integration/seam/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts closed-set fields are resolved by FR-B1, not by free-text LLM args.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A nonsensical practice-area × matter-type pair cannot commit via the grounded picker (negative test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size ≤60 MB; all tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-B3 / FR-B4; NFR-06 negative eval is authored in task 051.

    CLOSED 2026-07-16 as SATISFIED-BY-DESIGN (owner decision via AskUserQuestion). The task's scope is
    superseded by the task-002 SurfaceLaunch redesign + task-010 resolver; building it would be redundant
    (CLAUDE.md §11). Rationale, point by point:
    - "Exclude closed-set fields from LLM arg-filling" — ALREADY enforced: the create Actions emit LABELS
      (practice_area_suggestion / matter_type_suggestion), NOT GUIDs (task 002); allowstools=false blocks the
      LLM from resolving GUIDs or writing records; the WIZARD/FORM owns the closed-set write via real dropdowns.
      The capability input schema (BindingCapabilityTool → Binding.InputSchemaJson) already asks only for label
      hints — there is nothing to exclude.
    - "Closed-set fields resolved by FR-B1, not LLM args" — the resolver (010) does this; the actual WIRING of
      ResolveAsync into the draft→pre-seed path is task 013's job (where the resolver is called). A code
      assertion here would be premature/duplicative — it belongs with 013.
    - "Incoherent practice-area × matter-type pair cannot commit" — NO DATA-MODEL BASIS: verified 2026-07-16
      that sprk_mattertype_ref has NO practice-area relationship (independent reference table), so every PA×MT
      pair is independently valid at the schema level. There is no coherence table to enforce. "Only valid
      values commit" is guaranteed by the resolver (invalid label → none/low → picker) + the wizard's real
      dropdowns (cannot pick a nonexistent value).
    - Negative eval (incoherent combo) — belongs in the EVAL SUITE (task 051), not a unit test (catalog content
      is not unit-testable without hitting live Dataverse).
    Residual carried forward (not lost): (a) the resolver-wiring assertion → task 013; (b) the negative eval →
    task 051. No code produced. Publish-size/gates N/A (no code change).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge/files. /conflict-check before BFF PR. FULL-rigor Step 9.5.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
